description:
In src/wp11_proto_piv.c:129-134, piv_get_sw() does:
  *sw1 = resp[resplen - 2u];
  *sw2 = resp[resplen - 1u];
without bounds checking. If resplen < 2, the size_t arithmetic underflows, producing a huge index and an out-of-bounds read.

All current callers pre-validate resplen >= 2 before calling, so this is not currently exploitable. But the function has no contract annotation or internal guard, making it a latent bug for future callers.

Research: Audit all call sites to confirm every caller has the guard. Then either (a) add a precondition assert inside piv_get_sw, (b) have piv_get_sw return a bool and check it, or (c) add a comment documenting the mandatory precondition so future callers know.
